Step 1: Create ASP.NET Core Web API Project
         1. Open Visual Studio.
         2. Click Create New Project.
         3. Select ASP.NET Core Web API.
         4. Project Name: FactorialAPI
         5. Select .NET 8.
         6. Enable OpenAPI Support.
         7. Click Create.
Step 2: Create Controller
In Solution Explorer, create a class file:
Controllers/MathController.cs
Add the following code:
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc;
namespace FactorialAPI.Controllers
{
     [Route("api/[controller]")]
     [ApiController]
     public class MathController : ControllerBase
     {
          [HttpGet("factorial/{number}")]
          public IActionResult GetFactorial(int number)
          {
              if (number < 0)
             {
                 return BadRequest(
                   "Factorial not possible for negative numbers.");
             }
             long factorial = 1;
             for (int i = 1; i <= number; i++)
             {
                 factorial *= i;
             }
             return Ok(new
             {
                 Number = number,
                 Factorial = factorial
             });
         }
     }
}
Step 3: Run the Project
Run the project in Visual Studio.
The project will start, and a local URL will be displayed.
Example base URL:
https://localhost:7260
The port number may be different on your computer.
